// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/webapp_bridge.t27 -- the client half of an authenticated call, and the DTO
; mirror that has to stay shape-compatible with the server.
; The boundary is one browser tab. Inward from the host: where the proof of identity comes from,
; what it is worth, and what the client does in a tab that has no Telegram host at all. Outward
; to the server: what is attached to a request, what happens when one fails, whether a second
; attempt can become a second order, and how long a call may hang. Inward again from the wire:
; what a DTO does when the server stops sending a field. This file owns the CLIENT side of each
; of those and no server rule: whether a request PROVED who it is belongs to request_identity.t27,
; the read API's wire shape and numerals belong to catalog_api.t27, the idempotency verdict
; belongs to commerce.t27, what a customer is told when a call fails belongs to
; client_errors.t27, and which link lands where belongs to deeplink.t27. Five edges, named by ID
; below, not one of them restated.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). This half of the product has no compiler in the host test suite.
; src/lib.rs:17 gates `pub mod ui` on target_arch = "wasm32", so `cargo test` compiles none of it
; -- tests/money_is_never_invented.rs:10-16 says exactly that in its own words, and adds that the
; only other compiler, the wasm clippy gate, "has no opinion about unwrap_or(0.0)". The size of
; the blind spot is countable: src/ui holds FIVE `#[cfg(test)]` modules (src/ui/api/local_client.rs:181,
; src/ui/lang.rs:135, src/ui/screens/bike_detail.rs:572 (:570 until the 2026-09-25 edit that
; removed the all-taken line above it, and :600 until the 2026-09-24 rental-only edit removed the
; buy-out block above it), src/ui/screens/catalog_screen.rs:953 (:954 until the 2026-09-26 Book-control edit)
; (:599 and :966 until the 2026-09-24 availability edit, re-verified that day),
; src/ui/share.rs:409) containing THIRTY-TWO `#[test]` functions, and not one of the thirty-two is
; ever compiled, let alone run. The instrument that does exist is a text scan for four literal
; spellings of unwrap_or. A contract is the only other instrument available here, which is why the
; numbers below are line citations into src/ and never test names.
; The second number that forced the file: NINE call sites attach the identity header across the
; two transport modules, and SEVEN of the nine attach the label that tells the server which kind
; of client sent it. The two that omit it are named below.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Six corrections, each measured 2026-09-21. Three of the six were
; DEFECTS rather than miscounts, and all three were closed the same day; each is marked FIXED
; below and the old reading is kept beside the new one, because a correction nobody can compare
; with what it replaced is an assertion.
;   1. "src/ui/api/http.rs (582 lines - retry and timeout)" -- the file has neither. A
;      case-insensitive grep of src/ui/api/http.rs for retry returns 0 and for timeout returns 0,
;      across all 21 of its public functions. The only AUTOMATIC retry in the client half is
;      submit_order_with_retry at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:148 (:128 before the
;      2026-09-21 edits in items 4 and 5 below), it wraps exactly one
;      call, and it lives in a screen rather than in the transport. Three other screens carry a
;      retry BUTTON (src/ui/screens/events_screen.rs:924, src/ui/screens/profile_screen.rs:663,
;      src/ui/screens/success_screen.rs:479 -- :920, :659 and :476 before the same day's
;      cart-price edits moved them); those are a customer tap re-arming a resource, not
;      a re-send the code decides on, and they are counted separately. A request deadline does not
;      exist anywhere: AbortController, AbortSignal and .abort() return 0 occurrences over all of
;      src/ui. The twenty-two TimeoutFuture sites in src/ui are animation and polling delays; the
;      one inside the retry loop (:163, was :145) is backoff between attempts, not a bound on any attempt.
;   2. PARTLY FIXED 2026-09-21, and the superseded reading is kept beside the new one. The
;      mirror rule is not at risk, it is already refuted, and the count says by how much. Of
;      172 declared fields in src/ui/api/types.rs, 44 carry `#[serde(default)]` -- a plain
;      `grep -c` answers 45, because the comment at :37 names the attribute without being one, so
;      the count below is of attribute lines and not of matches (46 since 2c21df1 added the doc
;      line at :424, which names it too; re-measured 2026-09-22); 28 of those
;      default an Option, where absence stays absence, and SIX default a bare number, where
;      absence becomes a zero the server never sent. TWO of the six are the cart's own money
;      and counts: ServerCartItem.quantity (:423) and ServerCart.total (:450). (RE-POINTED
;      2026-09-24: :421 and :448 until DeliveryZone gained two attribute lines above them; the
;      DTO census below records that change. 44 and 28 are the 2026-09-22 counts, 46 and 30 now.)
;      SUPERSEDED READING, true until 2026-09-21: "27 of those default an Option ... and SEVEN
;      default a bare number ... Three of the seven are the cart's own money and counts:
;      ServerCartItem.quantity (:421), ServerCartItem.unit_price (:423) and ServerCart.total
;      (:435)." The third of those three is the defect this file's body records as fixed:
;      ServerCartItem.unit_price is an Option<f64> at :436 now, so absence arrives as absence
;      and not as a free line. The split moved 27/7 -> 28/6 while the total stayed 44 and the
;      field count stayed 172 -- one field changed type, none was added or removed, and
;      :435/:446 became :448/:459. MIRROR_RULE_HOLDS_ON_EVERY_FIELD is still false: a count
;      that fell by one is not a rule that now holds.
;   3. tests/money_is_never_invented.rs:11 cites the wasm gate as `src/lib.rs:16`. Line 16 is
;      blank; the attribute is at :17 and `pub mod ui;` at :18. The claim is right and the
;      citation is ONE line short of the attribute (two short of the module it gates). Recorded
;      because this file leans on that claim.
;   4. FIXED 2026-09-21. The reading this replaces: "The one place the client branches on a
;      duplicated write -- the 409 arm at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:162-178, whose own
;      comment at :125 calls 409 'already accepted' -- is written against a status
;      POST /api/orders never returns. The server answers a replay with 200 and a body flag
;      (src/api/orders.rs:1371-1375), refuses a malformed key with 400 (:876), and the only
;      StatusCode::CONFLICT in src/api/orders.rs is :2336 in cancel_order. The branch is
;      unreachable from the endpoint it guards."
;      The premise held and the arm is GONE rather than repaired: it recovered an order by
;      RECENCY, never matched against the idempotency key that was sent, and built its URL from
;      telegram_id.unwrap_or(0). A 409 now falls to the terminal arm and reaches the customer.
;      The premise is re-measured on every test run rather than quoted -- see
;      CONFLICT_PREMISE_IS_RE_MEASURED_BY_A_TEST and the REMOVED_ARM_ constants below. The
;      addresses in the quoted reading are the removed arm's, and nothing stands at :162-178
;      or :125 now.
;   5. FIXED 2026-09-21. The reading this replaces: "The retry's own doc comment miscounts it.
;      src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:124 says 'up to 3 attempts (delays 1s, 2s, 4s)', but
;      :140-141 chains one immediate attempt to the three delays, so the ceiling is four
;      requests and not three. The three delays are right; the attempt count is one short, and
;      a reader sizing the worst case from the comment misses one request in every four a
;      single tap can put on POST /api/orders."
;      The comment now says four (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:127) and names the day it
;      was corrected. The LOOP did not change: the ceiling was four before and is four now.
;      The old figure stays executable as ATTEMPTS_CLAIMED_BEFORE_2026_09_21, and
;      DOC_COMMENT_AGREES_WITH_THE_LOOP went false -> true.
;   6. The retry genuinely cannot duplicate a write, but not for a reason visible in the
;      transport. post_json_authed_idempotent_full (src/ui/api/http.rs:209) attaches whatever key
;      it is handed and mints none; the stability comes from the screen, where
;      `k.get_or_insert_with(|| uuid::Uuid::new_v4()...)` at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:971
;      (:934 before the same day's edits) is the file's only write to that signal. A reader who
;      audits the transport alone cannot
;      establish the property, and the same single write is why an edited cart re-submitted from a
;      mounted screen reuses the key with a different body.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It publishes no endpoint table: the route table is counted, not
; transcribed, and the path strings that do appear are the two that carry a measured defect. It
; invents no retry count for a call the code does not retry -- one call retries automatically,
; every other call in the transport makes a single attempt, the three manual retry buttons are
; counted as taps and not as re-sends, and that is stated as one and not as an unwritten
; policy. It declares no timeout, because none is implemented; the refusal is recorded instead of
; a plausible number. It re-declares no constant a sibling already holds: the idempotency header
; literal belongs to turbobaby/loyalty-ledger, the initData byte cap and its admission rule to
; turbobaby/request-identity, and this file names both owners rather than copying either value.
; It quotes no shipped string: the Russian comments in src/ui/api/types.rs:374-378 and
; src/ui/api/client.rs:299-305 (:262-268 before the 2026-09-21 edits) are cited by path and line
; and never reproduced. It carries no
; initData sample, real or synthetic, and no telegram id. Nothing from D14 -- no renter, handle,
; phone, key code, plate, debt, purchase price or personal note -- in a constant, a comment or a
; test.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-webapp-bridge;

pub const KIND : str = "client-contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/webapp-bridge";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby Mini App bridge, transport and DTO mirror";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";

; --- Sources --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const BRIDGE_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/telegram.rs";
pub const TRANSPORT_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/http.rs";
pub const DTO_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/types.rs";
pub const TYPED_CLIENT_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/client.rs";
pub const SHIM_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/local_client.rs";
pub const ROUTE_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/routes.rs";
pub const RETRY_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs";
pub const MIRROR_CONSUMER : str = "src/ui/state.rs";
pub const INSTRUMENT_WITNESS : str = "tests/money_is_never_invented.rs";
; wc -l over the tracked sources, so "the whole file" is a measurement. Re-measured 2026-09-21
; after the three client-side defects this file recorded were closed. Three of the six moved, and
; the sentence says which and by how much, because a length that changes silently is a length
; nobody re-read: transport 582 -> 601 (the merge DTO's price became an Option), DTO 454 -> 467
; (ServerCartItem.unit_price became an Option and carries the argument for it), typed client
; 305 -> 342 (the oversize refusal, and a named constructor for the anonymous client). The other
; three are untouched.
pub const BRIDGE_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 811;
